    "law": "Let theta be measured from the downward vertical. For a platform with constant upward acceleration a, theta_ddot = sin(theta)[Omega^2 cos(theta) - (g+a)/R]. The off-axis equilibrium satisfies cos(theta_0) = (g+a)/(Omega^2 R). Linearization gives omega_small^2 = Omega^2[1 - ((g+a)/(Omega^2 R))^2], and T = 2*pi/omega_small. Taking a=0 gives T=1.03646 s; taking a=2.1 m/s^2 gives T=1.12963 s.",
    "assumptions": [
      "The platform has no translational acceleration during the base observation; this condition is needed but not explicitly stated.",
      "The bead is treated as a point particle constrained to the rigid hoop.",
      "The motor maintains the stated angular speed during perturbations.",
      "Oscillations have sufficiently small amplitude for linearization."
    ],
